ity and saving rate data show multiple peaks across different time periods. Each metric has its own unique pattern of local maxima, ranging from 1 to 4 peaks depending on the specific economic indicator and time frame. The complexity arises from the varying economic cycles and trends within each dataset.\n\nI'll need to manually verify the chart details to confirm the precise number of local maxima, as the specific visual representation might differ from my initial estimates.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_48ec72d311984c9a91753ca6","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport json\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1990_09.json', 'r') as f:\n    data = json.load(f)\nelements = data['document']['elements']\n# Let's look for any table or structured data elements\n# that might contain actual plotted values\nfor i, e in enumerate(elements):\n    if e.get('type') == 'table':\n        content = e.get('content')\n        if content and 'saving' in str(content).lower()[:500]:\n            print(f'Table {i}:')\n            print(content[:500] if len(str(content)) > 500 else content)\n            print('---')\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
